y every other bone in his  body trying to pull this stunt  why couldn't he have just pushed zelda  out of the way or something  i mean damn link earlier in the story he  gets hit on the shield with a boulder  breaker and he flies like 20 feet  through the air into a wall but a solid  stone ceiling block 20 times his size  no biggie  [Music]  link what are you doing we have to hurry  the castle  it's about to collapse no worries  princess  check this out  oh wow that actually worked  there are some more of these little  moments spurred throughout the story  where i just can't ignore what i'm  seeing either because i know the  established lore  it's way too convenient as a plot device  or because it's just physically  impossible even within the fictional  world of zelda  now obviously i am nitpicking here and  hey maybe we're not supposed to think  about this stuff too much  and none of these points ultimately ruin  the experience for me by any means  but i do think it's fair to be critical  of a story and not just praise it  many of the negatives i've covered  probably won't bother the average player  or even be noticed by anyone aside from  those who are very knowledgeable and  invested in zelda lore  but even purely from a storytelling  perspective there were definitely some  things lacking  i think that astor for instance could  have been fleshed out more  it would have been nice to know why he  does what he does was he the fortune  teller who uttered the prophecy where  did he get the orb  why is he wearing gerudo clothing and  where did he get them  i also think they could have been a  little bit more clear about the fact  that ganon's malice corrupted the  present-day terrico when it followed  future terrico into the portal  not everything has to be explained in  detail but i can definitely see why some  people were confused about this part of  the narrative  a little cut scene showing the malice  taking him over and harbinger then  approaching astor for the first time and  showing him the future would have gone a  long way  anyway as not to end on a negative note  i will conclude with  the music the music kicks many asses  including mine what is there to say they  took the best and the most memorable  tracks which were already good in breath  of the wild and put them on steroids  these epic renditions are just  masterful some of my favorites being the  divine beast remixes the theme songs of  rivali and mifa  zelda's awakening and of course a fair  share of brand new tracks which all  sound great as well  they really outdid themselves here and  frankly there isn't much to say  other than a job well done for those who  thought breath of the wild lacked music  just put on the ost to age of calamity  next time you're playing that game  in conclusion though in no way as  amazing or groundbreaking as breath of  the wild  i think age of calamity is still a nice  addition to the series  for a game that came out of nowhere and  was released so quickly thereafter it  really gave me a fun experience to hold  me over until the next installment  and it was great to revisit this world  again and see it in a different light  getting to see the towns and settlements  still in their prime paired with some  fast-paced action and an  engaging story a story which in and of  itself is also harmless since in the  larger scheme of things  it doesn't invalidate or hurt the lore  established by breath of the wild  with the exception of the master sword  bit i mentioned earlier but that was  only given a backstory in creating a  champion which was written by a third  party nonetheless  other than that it doesn't change the  events of said game it might have an  impact on breath of the wild 2  story but we'll just have to wait and  see if that will be the case  and to what extent age of calamity is  not for everyone but  then again what game really is before we  close the curtains  i have a few things to note first off if  you haven't been follow